# Your documentation

facet app

This `index.work` is the **composition root** of a documentation site. It names the site and lists —
in order — the sections and pages the sidebar shows. Everything else is a sibling `.work` file of
plain prose. The nexus serves it live as a navigable site (sidebar + clean URLs); `work weave .`
folds the tree into one shippable artifact.

This starter ships **unstyled** — the nexus renders neutral, legible structure. To brand it, add a
sibling `design.work` with a `design` block; its CSS styles the site's `.wb-*` classes. (See the
Workbooks documentation template for a worked example.) Until then, `title` is all you set.

app :docs do
  title "Your Project"           # the site name (sidebar wordmark + tab title)

  section "Getting started" do
    page "getting-started/installation"
    page "getting-started/quickstart"
  end

  section "Guides" do
    page "guides/writing-pages"
  end
end
